    fix(cli): remember --wait flushes + awaits the namespace commit (CLI-WAIT-001)
    
    --wait was parsed but never consumed: every remember printed 'will be
    committed in batch' and the commit landed only via the process-exit
    flush, invisible to scripts that git-verify right after the call.
    
    - new waitForNamespaceCommit(namespacePath) in src/git/autocommit.ts:
      flushNamespaceCommit (forces the debounce window now, exit-path-only
      helper) + drainAsyncCommits-style settle detection scoped to one
      namespace's async chain (additive; serving paths untouched)
    - rememberCommand: with --wait, await the commit and print 'committed
      to git (namespace: <ns>)'; wait failures warn but never fail the
      write; without the flag the legacy buffered line is byte-identical
    - regression suite src/cli/remember-wait-cliwait001.test.ts drives the
      real CLI in a scratch root (env-redirected): committed+clean git
      state immediately after exit, legacy message preserved, no leak into
      namespaces/; RED control: reverting human.ts to HEAD fails it
    - AGENTS.md suite/test counts synced to live 158/1250
    
    GitReins: CLI-WAIT-001 (criteria in .gitreins/tasks.yaml)
